From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:10:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: aoc: alsa: refuse a PCM whose number is not its
 entry point

The PCM driver takes the AoC entry point of a playback stream, and the
use case of a capture stream, from the PCM device number. That holds
only when the card's DAI links are in the order of the stock device
tree, where EPn playback is PCM n - 1 and EPn capture PCM 8 + n - 1.

A card described by a device tree overlay had its links reversed (the
overlay apply inserts each new node first), so EP6 playback became PCM
47, and the AoC rejected it:

  F1: ERR: controller_audio_output.cc, 1912: Mode Playback is not supported by Entrypoint 47
  F1: ERR: controller_audio_output.cc, 2005: Entrypoint 47 cannot be configured

For the EP playback and capture links, check the PCM number against the
link id and refuse to open the PCM if they disagree, instead of
configuring some other entry point on the AoC.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_pcm.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_pcm.c b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_pcm.c
index c50d8e2d2..c5e3d2c3a 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_pcm.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/aoc/alsa/aoc_alsa_pcm.c
@@ -375,6 +375,29 @@ static int snd_aoc_pcm_open(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 
 	idx = substream->pcm->device;
 	pr_debug("pcm device open (%d)\n", idx);
+
+	/*
+	 * The AoC entry point (playback) and the capture use case are taken
+	 * from the PCM device number below, which is right only when the
+	 * card's DAI links are in the stock order, where the PCM number of a
+	 * front end follows from its link id: EPn playback (id n - 1) is PCM
+	 * n - 1, EPn capture (AOC_TX | n - 1) is PCM 8 + n - 1. Anything else
+	 * would configure some other entry point on the AoC, so refuse. (The
+	 * raw, ultrasonic and immersive links sit further down the stock list
+	 * with ids of their own; they are not checked.)
+	 */
+	if (!(rtd->dai_link->id & (AOC_BE | AOC_NOHOST)) &&
+	    AOC_ID_TO_INDEX(rtd->dai_link->id) < UC_AUDIO_RECORD) {
+		int expect = AOC_ID_TO_INDEX(rtd->dai_link->id) +
+			     ((rtd->dai_link->id & AOC_TX) ? UC_AUDIO_RECORD : 0);
+
+		if (expect != idx) {
+			pr_err("%s is PCM %d, expected PCM %d: the card's DAI links are not in the stock order\n",
+			       rtd->dai_link->name, idx, expect);
+			mutex_unlock(&chip->audio_mutex);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+	}
 	pr_debug("chip open (%llu)\n", chip->opened);
 
 	alsa_stream = kzalloc(sizeof(struct aoc_alsa_stream), GFP_KERNEL);
